(102099, 4276, 3080, '<td valign="top">I read in a tutorial that if you can''t get it centered exactly, to not center it, but to use the rule of thirds.  I think that may make this more visually interesting.  The clarity is great, and I like how it stands out from the background.  Some people are probably going to say it''s too "OOF"  in the background but I personally like it exactly how it is.  The title is very orriginal, I like it.  A lot better than "New flower" lol.  I wonder if it were open just a little bit more, if it may have a bit more color, in contrast to all the green.  Great job with your photo.  Good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'I read in a tutorial that if you can''t get it centered exactly, to not center it, but to use the rule of thirds.  I think that may make this more visually interesting.  The clarity is great, and I like how it stands out from the background.  Some people are probably going to say it''s too "OOF"  in the background but I personally like it exactly how it is.  The title is very orriginal, I like it.  A lot better than "New flower" lol.  I wonder if it were open just a little bit more, if it may have a bit more color, in contrast to all the green.  Great job with your photo.  Good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-16 22:47:00.000000', NULL, 1),
