(102540, 4308, 3087, '<td valign="top">Interesting building and the cloud is great - it looks very surreal and cartoony, I don''t know how you did that. Increase of contrast?<br/>I''d like just a little more of the building in the shot, not much but a bit. There''s just a little too much blue at the top half.<br/>5, Kavey</td>', 'Interesting building and the cloud is great - it looks very surreal and cartoony, I don''t know how you did that. Increase of contrast?I''d like just a little more of the building in the shot, not much but a bit. There''s just a little too much blue at the top half.5, Kavey', '2002-08-13 18:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(102541, 4308, 737, '<td valign="top">Something new. <br/>Composition - pretty good<br/>Technical Aspects - pretty good. <br/>Meets Challenge - yes, I assume so<br/>Visual Impact / Originality  pretty good<br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Something new. Composition - pretty goodTechnical Aspects - pretty good. Meets Challenge - yes, I assume soVisual Impact / Originality  pretty goodJim msp', '2002-08-13 23:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(102542, 4308, 3080, '<td valign="top">Hey!  I think this is the "rule of thirds"!  I don''t much know about the rule of thirds, only what I read in the threads in the forums, but I think that rule was applied here, and it IS pretty appealing.  You did an excelent job of making that building straight in the photo.  The edge of the photo goes right along the cross bar of the window.  I also like how you made it so the skyline was new, and not the building.  That is very creative and has a really neat affect.  Plus that sky is a beautiful blue.  The cloud may be a slight bit too bright, but that was probably nessasary in order to make the building not too dark.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'Hey!  I think this is the "rule of thirds"!  I don''t much know about the rule of thirds, only what I read in the threads in the forums, but I think that rule was applied here, and it IS pretty appealing.  You did an excelent job of making that building straight in the photo.  The edge of the photo goes right along the cross bar of the window.  I also like how you made it so the skyline was new, and not the building.  That is very creative and has a really neat affect.  Plus that sky is a beautiful blue.  The cloud may be a slight bit too bright, but that was probably nessasary in order to make the building not too dark.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-15 13:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(102543, 4308, 637, '<td valign="top">Very effective shot... great catch... beautiful sky, beautiful architecture 7 sjgleah</td>', 'Very effective shot... great catch... beautiful sky, beautiful architecture 7 sjgleah', '2002-08-18 05:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(102544, 4308, 3112, '<td valign="top">Excellent sky, coloration and detail.  Building is slightly off-axis w/respect to the <br/>whole composition.  Very Good overall.</td>', 'Excellent sky, coloration and detail.  Building is slightly off-axis w/respect to the whole composition.  Very Good overall.', '2002-08-18 19:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
