(103766, 4395, 2337, '<td valign="top">I''m curious as to how this meets the challenge... I will revisit this later in the week to see if I''m missing something.  Feel free to PM me if I''m missing something obvious here. ~ myqyl ~ <br/><br/>Thanks for the insight... I can see where you were headed... I don''t think you got there, but I definitely see where you were heading...</td>', 'I''m curious as to how this meets the challenge... I will revisit this later in the week to see if I''m missing something.  Feel free to PM me if I''m missing something obvious here. ~ myqyl ~ Thanks for the insight... I can see where you were headed... I don''t think you got there, but I definitely see where you were heading...', '2002-08-12 22:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103767, 4395, 671, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait.  A little weak on the challenge.</td>', 'Nice portrait.  A little weak on the challenge.', '2002-08-13 14:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103768, 4395, 737, '<td valign="top">Something new. <br/>Composition - good<br/>Technical Aspects - good<br/>Meets Challenge - not clear to me<br/>Visual Impact / Originality  good<br/>Jim msp<br/></td>', 'Something new. Composition - goodTechnical Aspects - goodMeets Challenge - not clear to meVisual Impact / Originality  goodJim msp', '2002-08-13 19:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103769, 4395, 3080, '<td valign="top">Is the something new suposed to be the sunset reflected in the glasses?  I don''t think people usually view a sun set as something new, however in a stretch, it could be viewed as a new night.  I thought maybe the something new was the haircut, but then thought that if it was the haircut, than that would have been incooperated into the title.   Setting that aside, the photo may have had better impact if the sunset reflected into the glasses was straight across the glasses instead of at an angle.  The fact that it''s all crooked makes it look more like a candid photo rather than a well thought out artistic photo.  Another way to make this seem less candid and more thought out would be to straighten the shirt near the collar and find a more pleasing background.  The pretty sunset is kind of washed out by the chain fence and dead grass.  I do get from the title that if this was a "brief" encounter with the guy, than maybe you didn''t have the opportunity to go through the trouble to ask him to move to a more pretty spot, tilt his head and straighten his shirt.  And, if you didn''t know him, this would be almost impossible to accomplish for the feeling of asking too much of a person you don''t even know.  I think that if you went back and tried this again, when you have more time to get a good really shot of it (posed with someone you knew and that would be patient for you to get a good shot), then it would have a really great effect.  it''s a great idea, don''t ever give up and good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'Is the something new suposed to be the sunset reflected in the glasses?  I don''t think people usually view a sun set as something new, however in a stretch, it could be viewed as a new night.  I thought maybe the something new was the haircut, but then thought that if it was the haircut, than that would have been incooperated into the title.   Setting that aside, the photo may have had better impact if the sunset reflected into the glasses was straight across the glasses instead of at an angle.  The fact that it''s all crooked makes it look more like a candid photo rather than a well thought out artistic photo.  Another way to make this seem less candid and more thought out would be to straighten the shirt near the collar and find a more pleasing background.  The pretty sunset is kind of washed out by the chain fence and dead grass.  I do get from the title that if this was a "brief" encounter with the guy, than maybe you didn''t have the opportunity to go through the trouble to ask him to move to a more pretty spot, tilt his head and straighten his shirt.  And, if you didn''t know him, this would be almost impossible to accomplish for the feeling of asking too much of a person you don''t even know.  I think that if you went back and tried this again, when you have more time to get a good really shot of it (posed with someone you knew and that would be patient for you to get a good shot), then it would have a really great effect.  it''s a great idea, don''t ever give up and good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-14 01:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103770, 4395, 2798, '<td valign="top">Doesnt quite get enough of the sunset reflected in the glasses. Great smile though.</td>', 'Doesnt quite get enough of the sunset reflected in the glasses. Great smile though.', '2002-08-14 07:58:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103771, 4395, 917, '<td valign="top">Good portrait, but the background is a bit ugly.</td>', 'Good portrait, but the background is a bit ugly.', '2002-08-14 13:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(103772, 4395, 1005, '<td valign="top">Wow, you must be on another etherical plane from me, I just don''t understand this at all.  NEW?  New what?  New friend?  His first smile, first shave, first sunglasses, new ear ring?  I give up.  6 Swash (sooo tempted to further downgrade....)</td>', 'Wow, you must be on another etherical plane from me, I just don''t understand this at all.  NEW?  New what?  New friend?  His first smile, first shave, first sunglasses, new ear ring?  I give up.  6 Swash (sooo tempted to further downgrade....)', '2002-08-14 17:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
