(104238, 4414, 3044, '<td valign="top">very nice. i love this. i like the non traditional placement and the angle. nice colors. i hope you dont get slammed because this isnt a typical product shot. good luck.</td>', 'very nice. i love this. i like the non traditional placement and the angle. nice colors. i hope you dont get slammed because this isnt a typical product shot. good luck.', '2002-08-15 12:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104239, 4414, 3080, '<td valign="top">Took me awhile to tell exactly what I was looking at here.  I''m still not 100% sure, but looks like ear rings?  I get the point of them being a  birthday present making them new, but was there a box they came in?  The bottom of the photo is pretty fuzzy.  This could have been minimalized with a vertical shot rather than a diagnal shot.  The glare from the lighting source is a little much, could you have bounced the flash?  I know it''s not possible to do that with my camera, so I can relate to exaggerated reflection.  Something that I found that helped out my photos is to take the photo outside and use a thin white canopy between the sun and the subject.  Or if the photo is taken indoors, put a thin tissue paper or cheesecloth between the light source and the subject.  I even got a desirable result from taping a thin piece of white cloth directly onto the flash on my camera.  Seemed to spread the light out a bit and make it less reflective in the photo.  I liked the idea behind this photo very much and gave it above average rating.  Great job and good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Took me awhile to tell exactly what I was looking at here.  I''m still not 100% sure, but looks like ear rings?  I get the point of them being a  birthday present making them new, but was there a box they came in?  The bottom of the photo is pretty fuzzy.  This could have been minimalized with a vertical shot rather than a diagnal shot.  The glare from the lighting source is a little much, could you have bounced the flash?  I know it''s not possible to do that with my camera, so I can relate to exaggerated reflection.  Something that I found that helped out my photos is to take the photo outside and use a thin white canopy between the sun and the subject.  Or if the photo is taken indoors, put a thin tissue paper or cheesecloth between the light source and the subject.  I even got a desirable result from taping a thin piece of white cloth directly onto the flash on my camera.  Seemed to spread the light out a bit and make it less reflective in the photo.  I liked the idea behind this photo very much and gave it above average rating.  Great job and good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-15 13:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104240, 4414, 2700, '<td valign="top">Interesting photo, very artistic 8</td>', 'Interesting photo, very artistic 8', '2002-08-16 00:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
