(104506, 4432, 3105, '<td valign="top">This is pretty well done.  I like the water droplets hanging off the tomatoes and throwing the background out of focus helps to emphasize the nicely rounded, wet tomato up front.  It''s difficult to get a good photo when so much of the frame has roughly the same tones and this is a good job.<br/>Score: 7<br/>Courtenay</td>', 'This is pretty well done.  I like the water droplets hanging off the tomatoes and throwing the background out of focus helps to emphasize the nicely rounded, wet tomato up front.  It''s difficult to get a good photo when so much of the frame has roughly the same tones and this is a good job.Score: 7Courtenay', '2002-08-14 15:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104507, 4432, 2173, '<td valign="top">nice!!!! 10</td>', 'nice!!!! 10', '2002-08-14 18:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104508, 4432, 3080, '<td valign="top">I love the focus on the front tomato.  Great detail with that fuzzy stem.  The water is a cool effect, but may be a little distracting from the tomato.  I look at it and automatically look down to the water, only to see the distorted image of the pole in the background.  My eyes then follow the actual pole in the background right off the picture, and then I''m not looking at the "something new" anymore.  The pole definately bothers me, but you have still captured a really great photo here.  And there is definately newness.  Maybe try that "rule of thirds" everyone is talking about.  Not sure how it works, but heard that it''s visually appealing.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'I love the focus on the front tomato.  Great detail with that fuzzy stem.  The water is a cool effect, but may be a little distracting from the tomato.  I look at it and automatically look down to the water, only to see the distorted image of the pole in the background.  My eyes then follow the actual pole in the background right off the picture, and then I''m not looking at the "something new" anymore.  The pole definately bothers me, but you have still captured a really great photo here.  And there is definately newness.  Maybe try that "rule of thirds" everyone is talking about.  Not sure how it works, but heard that it''s visually appealing.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-15 03:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104509, 4432, 2928, '<td valign="top">This is a really great shot, it really captures the newness</td>', 'This is a really great shot, it really captures the newness', '2002-08-15 06:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104510, 4432, 2881, '<td valign="top">Love the droplets on the tomato in the foreground, but would like to see more clarity on the two tomatoes right behind, although I realize that can be hard to achieve.  I find the fuzziness of the background kind of distracting so I might have cropped this a bit more... again, I don''t know how much you had to work with, and have often had to settle for something less than I thought perfect because I simply didn''t have enough to work with in the original.</td>', 'Love the droplets on the tomato in the foreground, but would like to see more clarity on the two tomatoes right behind, although I realize that can be hard to achieve.  I find the fuzziness of the background kind of distracting so I might have cropped this a bit more... again, I don''t know how much you had to work with, and have often had to settle for something less than I thought perfect because I simply didn''t have enough to work with in the original.', '2002-08-15 11:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104511, 4432, 327, '<td valign="top">Well done. Score-7 Kee</td>', 'Well done. Score-7 Kee', '2002-08-15 17:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(104512, 4432, 806, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.</td>', 'Beautiful shot.', '2002-08-15 17:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
