(105079, 4460, 3105, '<td valign="top">This is a pretty good photo although I don''t know if b&amp;w is the best option (color would be nice if the grasses were green and on the light conditions were favorable).  Another reason is that the contrast in b&amp;w is really low with a small range of greys and in color the contrast should be less noticable because you''re getting more than just different shades of one tone (grey).  I would also be interestd to see how the composition would look framed vertically, especially if it allowed for any sky to be seen at the top of the frame which could help with the contrast if it were still in b&amp;w.<br/>Score: 5<br/>Courtenay</td>', 'This is a pretty good photo although I don''t know if b&w is the best option (color would be nice if the grasses were green and on the light conditions were favorable).  Another reason is that the contrast in b&w is really low with a small range of greys and in color the contrast should be less noticable because you''re getting more than just different shades of one tone (grey).  I would also be interestd to see how the composition would look framed vertically, especially if it allowed for any sky to be seen at the top of the frame which could help with the contrast if it were still in b&w.Score: 5Courtenay', '2002-08-14 16:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(105080, 4460, 3266, '<td valign="top">hmmm...I like it.....</td>', 'hmmm...I like it.....', '2002-08-14 23:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
