(105464, 4478, 3080, '<td valign="top">I see the humor, but it''s really only the title that gives much reference to the challenge "something new".  Granted, I could probably go so far as to say that it''s new dirt, then it meets the challenge.  However, setting that aside, it''s still not really visually appealing.  Funny, yes.  Something I could look at for hours, no.  The lighting is great, no funny shadows and nothing too bright on the subject.  Only lighting flaw I see is your shadow.  Maybe the photo could have been taken at a different time of day so it didn''t show your shadow.  If not, cropping is always an option.  It is as a location where you wouldn''t lose anything from your photo if you just sliced off the bottom a bit.  You have great focus, with nice detail.  I love the bird way in the back between the 2 highest trees.  Good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'I see the humor, but it''s really only the title that gives much reference to the challenge "something new".  Granted, I could probably go so far as to say that it''s new dirt, then it meets the challenge.  However, setting that aside, it''s still not really visually appealing.  Funny, yes.  Something I could look at for hours, no.  The lighting is great, no funny shadows and nothing too bright on the subject.  Only lighting flaw I see is your shadow.  Maybe the photo could have been taken at a different time of day so it didn''t show your shadow.  If not, cropping is always an option.  It is as a location where you wouldn''t lose anything from your photo if you just sliced off the bottom a bit.  You have great focus, with nice detail.  I love the bird way in the back between the 2 highest trees.  Good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-18 02:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
